      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is partially done. This [line](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/5838354/21/zephyr/Kconfig.rsa#85) always evaluates to zero when I don\u0027t explicity set PLATFORM_EC_RWSIG_READ_ADDR in prj.conf. I\u0027ve tried a few different variations, not found the right one yet. Additionally, in order to calculate the correct mapped storage address in Kconfig by default, think we\u0027d need to add a mapped_storage_offset or similar to the binman structure, is that what you had in mind? Alternately, I can set the values in prj.conf for helipilot but have so far only found a hacky, hard-coded solution for (this)[https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/5018794/45/zephyr/program/fpmcu/helipilot/prj.conf#46]. What looks like a cleaner [solution](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/5018794/45/zephyr/program/fpmcu/helipilot/prj.conf#51) doesn\u0027t compile. Suggestions welcome",
